Feature: Generated story ideas are Items at the idea stage
  The newsroom generates story ideas: a monitor finds a page, a weekly snapshot shows a trend, a synthesis run links several References.
  Each idea is filed as a content Item at the idea stage, the same stage a person's idea starts at. The Item records in its front matter that
  a machine made it, by which run and monitor, and what it cites. Every Reference it cites is linked to it as the story it is based on, so
  the Reference counts as covered whatever an editor then does: accepting moves the Item forward, declining moves it to spiked with a reason.
  A body that copies a cited Reference's text is refused before anything is written. Filing the same idea twice finds the Item that is
  already there. Story drafts that were filed as Proposals before ideas became Items are converted once, by an editor, in a dry run first.

  Background:
    Given a Reference "Clef decision models" with captured text

  Scenario: An idea is filed as an Item at the idea stage that says a machine made it
    When the pipeline files an idea citing the Reference
    Then the Item is at the idea stage and is a draft
    And the Item records that it was generated by AI from the "hn" monitor
    And the Item is linked to the Reference as "based_on"
    And the Item's body has no drafting bookkeeping line

  Scenario: The same idea is never filed twice
    When the pipeline files an idea citing the Reference
    And the pipeline files an idea citing the Reference
    Then exactly 1 Item exists

  Scenario: An idea that copies the Reference is refused
    When the pipeline files an idea whose body repeats the Reference's captured text
    Then the filing is refused because the body is copied from the Reference
    And no Item exists

  Scenario: A declined idea still counts as drafted
    Given the pipeline filed an idea citing the Reference
    When an editor moves the idea to spiked saying "not our kind of story"
    Then the idea pipeline treats the Reference as already drafted

  Scenario: Open story draft Proposals are converted once, after a dry run
    Given these story draft Proposals:
      | id     | state    | cites     | filed      |
      | prop-a | draft    | the Clef  | 2026-10-30 |
      | prop-b | draft    | the Clef  | 2026-10-31 |
      | prop-c | declined | the Clef  | 2026-10-29 |
    When the editor runs the migration without writing
    Then the plan converts "prop-a", skips "prop-b" as a duplicate and skips "prop-c" as decided
    And no Item exists
    When the editor runs the migration with writing
    Then exactly 1 Item exists at the idea stage
    And running the plan again skips "prop-a" because it is already covered

  Scenario: An idea whose text breaks an error-severity editorial policy is not filed
    Given the site's editorial check finds an error violation of "production-claims" and a warning
    When the pipeline files an idea citing the Reference
    Then the filing is refused and the reason names "production-claims"
    And no Item exists

  Scenario: Warnings travel with the idea and its check is stored
    Given the site's editorial check finds only a warning
    When the pipeline files an idea citing the Reference
    Then the Item keeps 1 warning in its check result
    And the check is stored as the Item's check run

  Scenario: A judgment lane that could not run is recorded, never passed silently
    Given the judgment lane is unavailable because no TYPESAFE_API_KEY is set
    When the pipeline files an idea citing the Reference
    Then the Item's check says the judgment lane did not run and why

  Scenario: Cleaner ideas come first in the batch review
    Given three ideas with no findings, one warning and one note
    Then the review lists them in that order: no findings, then the note, then the warning

  Scenario: A morning batch of generated ideas appears in the Idea column and its review request links there
    Given three ideas filed in one morning run
    When the run raises its review request
    Then all three ideas are in the Idea column of the Stories board
    And exactly one review request is open for the run, and its links are those three ideas as stories
    And no Proposal is filed for any of them
    And the review request tells the editor to move an idea forward to accept it or to Spiked with a reason to decline it

  Scenario: Accepting an idea is moving it forward and declining it is spiking it with a reason
    Given three ideas filed in one morning run
    When an editor moves the first idea forward to "reporting" and spikes the second saying "Too basic for our readers"
    Then the first and second ideas have left the Idea column and the third is still in it
    And the pipeline's feedback holds an accept for the first idea and a decline with the reason for the second
    And the third idea has no decision yet

  Scenario: An idea can name the earlier ideas it replaces
    Given the pipeline filed an idea citing the Reference
    When a roundup idea that supersedes it is filed
    Then the roundup records the earlier idea's lineage as superseded

  Scenario: An editor's decisions on ideas are labels for the idea pipeline and a Cyclotron
    Given three generated ideas: one the editor moved forward, one the editor spiked saying "Too basic for our readers", and one still waiting
    Then the pipeline's feedback holds an accept and a decline with the reason, and nothing for the waiting idea
    And the Cyclotron export has an include row and an exclude row that carry the reason and the cited Reference
    And no Message was written
